{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And a he-goat, etc.</b> All the he-goats of the additional offerings come to atone for defilement of the Sanctuary and its holy things — all as explained in tractate Shavuot (page 9). And the he-goat of the new moon differs, for 'לַה'\" is stated of it — to teach you that it atones for a matter in which there is no knowledge, neither at the beginning nor at the end, for none recognizes the sin but the Holy One, blessed be He, alone; and the other he-goats learn from it. And its midrash in the Aggadah: the Holy One, blessed be He, said: Bring atonement for Me, for I diminished the moon (Chulin 60a)." "<b>Beside the burnt-offering of the daily morning-offering it shall be done.</b> The entire offering [is meant]." "<b>And its drink-offering.</b> 'וְנִסְכוֹ' is not governed by the he-goat, for a sin-offering has no drink-offerings."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:10.392304656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}